 "review": "independent read-only review of the first version: approve with nits — success is byte- and mask-identical to the per-seat loops (write's no-op return, makeFlatUnique's copy or cache clear, sharing kept when nothing changes); every refusal precedes any mutation; the dense table equals the dictionary for every UInt32; no exclusivity overlap. Nits applied before the gate: a test of the unique, cached production path, parted records unchanged, a lookup test against the dictionary, the overflow-safe range guard, one table index. The stepped table (after the probe) keeps the same contract and is covered by the lookup test",
 "review_stepped_table": "independent read-only review of TokenOrdinals after the probe: correct — equals the dictionary for every UInt32 token and every unique token list (incl. empty and single-token): the step divides every distance so slots never collide; a wrapped distance below the lowest token exceeds high - low, so a wrapped multiple of any step lands past the table; ordinals never reach the .max sentinel. Test gaps (probes for wrapped multiples at the large steps, high + step, the empty list, the 65,536-slot boundary) are added in a later commit"
}
